{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.151,
   "text": "I stock shelves overnight at a grocery store on the edge of town."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.751,
   "end": 12.591,
   "text": "Twelve aisles. Humming lights. And nobody else... ever."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 13.391,
   "end": 17.017,
   "text": "My manager gave me one rule on my first shift."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 17.617,
   "end": 23.42,
   "text": "If the intercom ever pages you to aisle thirteen... don't go. Just clock out, and leave."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 24.22,
   "end": 27.996,
   "text": "For two months, that intercom never made a sound."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 28.696,
   "end": 32.429,
   "text": "Then, last night, at three a.m.... it crackled."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 35.029,
   "end": 39.424,
   "text": "A soft voice. Almost kind. Cleanup... on aisle thirteen."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 40.624,
   "end": 45.125,
   "text": "I looked down the row of signs. One through twelve. Like always."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 45.725,
   "end": 53.0,
   "text": "But past the freezers, at the far back wall, a thirteenth sign was swinging... over a dark aisle I had never seen."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.0,
   "end": 57.648,
   "text": "I didn't go. I clocked out, and ran for the doors."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.148,
   "end": 59.577,
   "text": "They wouldn't open."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 61.777,
   "end": 66.94,
   "text": "Behind me, one by one, the aisle lights started going dark... coming closer."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 67.94,
   "end": 71.801,
   "text": "I backed into the last lit aisle, right by the doors."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 73.201,
   "end": 77.191,
   "text": "And the soft voice came back... Cleanup... on aisle one."
  }
 ],
